==== Factory Restore ====
-> [[docs:guide-user:installation:generic.uninstall]]

{{page>meta:infobox:dangerous&noheader&nofooter&noeditbtn}}

With the TL-WR842ND router, there is a catch: the stock firmware is obtained from the OEM: http://www.tplink.com/en/support/download/?model=TL-WDR3320

The OpenWrt firmware is now in progress on [[http://www.right.com.cn/forum/forum.php?mod=viewthread&tid=141401&page=1]]

But it seems the offical firmware comes with a different RSA signature, so the head of modded OpenWrt firmware is different that can only be write with a third-party u-boot or a SPI programmer, but not the offical flash web pages.

maybe this method would work if the firmware is chinese? [[https://forum.openwrt.org/viewtopic.php?pid=339567#p339567]]

The modded source code is here: [[https://code.csdn.net/hackpascal/openwrt/tree/master]]

